# Firebase Cloud Functions environment variables (example).
# Copy to `functions/.env` (gitignored) and fill in the values. Firebase reads it at
# deploy time; without it the deploy still succeeds but features that read the variable
# stay disabled. Values here are shared by every project (prod and staging).

# Shared key gating the keepWarm scheduler's `__warmup` short-circuit
# (functions/src/scheduled/keepWarm.ts). An unauthenticated caller must not be able to
# earn a 200 from a warmed callable by sending `__warmup: true`, so the target only
# short-circuits when this key matches. A low-sensitivity shared value is enough:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# When empty, the short-circuit is disabled (fail closed) and keepWarm skips its pings,
# so the hot callables pay cold starts again (~1.3-4s).
WARMUP_KEY=
